  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Please implement a system where friends can override your ear muffs. Essentially this toggle will help tune out non-friends outside the designated proximity.\n\nHere is a scenario where this would be handy: You're in a crowded instance, mostly non-friends. Your earmuffs are on, and you're having that conversation with somebody. Your friend is trying to get your attention, but she doesn't know that you have earmuffs on.\n\nThere are a few reasons how this could happen.\n\n-Your friend plays VRChat with nameplates off.\n\n-Your friend isn't aware that the earmuffs icon is on your nameplate; it could be small and hard to miss sometimes.\n\n-Your friend doesn't know what the icon on the nameplate means, so they don't pay any regard to it.\n\nThis toggle can be used to prioritize hearing friends, or for people who have problems with processing sound like me. Sometimes it's awkward to call a friend over close to you in a loud chatty instance, or if you walk over to your friend and there's other people standing right next to them also chatting, making it hard to hear.",
